---
import release from '../data/release';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const glow=Object.values(release.platforms).find(item=>item&&!item.legacy);
---
<article class="content">
 <p class="eyebrow">{glow?`GlowTV ${glow.version} · Published release`:'In development · GlowTV rebrand'}</p>
 <h2>What’s new in GlowTV</h2>
 <ul><li>GlowTV display name, supplied launcher artwork and leaf-green styling.</li><li>Native phone navigation, sheets and accessible press feedback.</li><li>A dedicated TV rail, featured live content and compact guide.</li><li>App and website separated into independent projects.</li><li>Original demo scenes, platform guides and provider help.</li><li>Existing profiles, playback engines, backups and transition settings retained.</li></ul>
 <p>{glow?'Published GlowTV downloads are listed by platform below. Each release links to its exact version notes and files.':'These are source changes; the new GlowTV binaries are not published yet.'}</p>
 <a class="text-link" href="/changelog/rss.xml">Subscribe to the updates feed (RSS)</a>
 <h2>Published releases</h2><p>Choose an edition for its version-specific release notes.</p>
 <div class="release-links">{Object.entries(release.platforms).map(([edition,item])=>item&&<a href={item.source}>{edition==='ios'?'iPhone':edition==='tv'?'TV':'Android'} {item.version} release notes <Icon name="external" size={15}/></a>)}</div>
 <a href="https://github.com/nhshajib/NodeCast/releases">View the complete project release history <Icon name="external" size={15}/></a>
</article>
